  "goodToKnow": "Ahnen means to suspect or sense: Ich ahne Schlimmes. The noun die Ahnung is a hunch or an idea, and Keine Ahnung! is the everyday way to say I've no idea. Ahnungslos means clueless. Careful: die Ahnen (plural) are ancestors, an elevated word from der Ahn, and Ahnenforschung is genealogy. Whether the two words are related historically is debated, so remember them as two words."
